    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕnălippus</span></b>  (orig. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlănip-pus</span></b> ),
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μελάνιππος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the slayer of Tydeus, who, while dying, bit the head
				of Menalippus</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 8, 719</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">740</span></i>.—The form Melanippus is found as <i>the name of a tragedy of Attius</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				3, 9, 20</span></i>.</div>
